🚗 Day 17/60 — Vehicle Cost Analysis Dashboard
A single-file, dark-themed dashboard that reads real trip data and computes the true running cost of five fuel types — Petrol, Diesel, CNG, EV, and E85 — for a Honda Civic (CNG, mixed driving, 1,000 km/month).
Built as part of my 60-Day Claude AI Challenge.
🔍 What it does
Parses a CSV of 95 logged trips and groups them by fuel type to compute cost/km, CO₂/km, maintenance/km, and average refuel time
Buckets the data by car age (New 0–2y, Mid-life 3–5y, Aged 6–9y, Old 10+y) to show how running cost changes over time
Fits a linear regression per fuel type to project cost/km across 0–12 years and plots it as an SVG line chart
Solves the "E85 Paradox": E85 is cheaper per litre at the pump, but its poor mileage means it actually costs more per km to run than petrol — quantified with pump-saving %, running-penalty %, and a break-even price
Scores E85 out of 10 (cost = 4pt, CO₂ = 3pt, refuel time = 2pt, maintenance = 1pt) using min–max normalization against the other four fuels, shown on an animated tachometer-style gauge
🛠️ Built with
Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript — no frameworks, no chart libraries, no CDN
All charts (bar, doughnut, line, gauge) are hand-built pure SVG, generated dynamically from the parsed CSV
Glassmorphism UI on a dark navy base, with hover tooltips on every chart segment
Fully responsive, 375px (mobile) to 1440px (desktop)
